// CROWN — latency rides a structural record ARGUMENT into an open-row
// parameter: `use({run: loud})` where `use(r) = r.run()`, under `with !E`.
// Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Refuses through the pinned boot. The guard on the record helpers: the
// open-against-closed meeting names its sides in a fixed order whichever is
// the value, so a flow read off that order would run context into value
// and lose the perform.
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn loud() = op()
fn use(r) = r.run()
fn bad() with !E = use({run: loud})
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = bad() ~> h
